(By Sid)Explanation of how shear is computed and how shear calibration from
metadetection is used.
slack: https://roman-hlis-cosmology.slack.com/archives/C0B6S0ZRKFG/p1782158187678359?thread_ts=1780773721.282879&cid=C0B6S0ZRKFG
- To do shear calibration with metadetection, we apply a shear to the image before detection and object measurement.
  ns: no shear is applied
  1p: (+0.01, 0.00)
  2p: (0.00, +0.01)
  1m: (-0.01, 0.00)
  2m: (0.00, -0.01)

  instead of forcing matches between these catalogs, the mean shear response is computed based on
  (<1p> - <1m>) / (2 * 0.01) or
  (<2p> - <2m>) / (2 * 0.01)
  and that can be used to calibrate the mean shear from <ns>


